=== ARZ-coded services ===

The ARZ code is used for flights where all passengers are ticketed to the [[International City of Areza]]. Any airline may operate ARZ-coded flights from the Areza Concourse of Terminal C, provided that all passengers on the flight hold confirmed onward travel to Areza. In practice, ARZ-coded flights are operated primarily by the flag carriers of [[Adonian Community]] member states, reflecting the AC's role as the principal destination for diplomatic, institutional, and official travel to Areza. Passengers on ARZ-coded flights clear Areza customs and immigration within the Areza Concourse and are transported to Areza via the [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Metro Line 9]] express service, which operates non-stop between the airport and Areza station in approximately 45 minutes. The ARZ arrangement eliminates the need for passengers travelling to Areza to clear Balboan customs or meet Balboan visa requirements, streamlining the connection between international flights and the AC institutions. This is of particular importance because Areza maintains a 15-day open visa policy for all [[Adonian Community]] member states, whereas Balboa applies its own separate visa requirements — meaning that nationals of AC member states who would require a Balboan visa for transit through the main terminals can travel to Areza via ARZ-coded flights without restriction.

== Ground transport ==

=== Metro ===

{{main|Metro de Sant Cristòfor}}

[[File:Sant Cristofor Airport Metro Transit Centre station placeholder.jpg|thumb|250px|The Airport Transit Centre Metro station, beneath the central atrium]]

The airport is served by two lines of the [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor]]:

[[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Line 1]] connects the airport to the city centre via the [[Grand Train Terminal]]. The airport extension operates an express service from the airport to the edge of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], skipping intermediate stops, before running local for the final 7 km through Original's dense urban core. The journey time from the airport to the Grand Train Terminal is approximately 20 minutes. All-stations services also operate on the same tracks at a lower frequency.

[[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Line 9]] connects the airport to the [[International City of Areza|International City of Areza]] via the canal corridor, a distance of 51.2 km, with a journey time of approximately 45 minutes on the express service. Line 9 was built with bypass tracks at all intermediate stations, allowing express services to skip local stops and provide a direct connection between the airport and Areza. The express service operates every 10 minutes during peak hours and every 15 minutes off-peak; all-stations services operate on the same tracks at a lower frequency.

The airport has two Metro stations. Line 1 serves the '''Airport Transit Centre''' station, located beneath the central atrium with direct access to all terminals. Line 9 splits at a junction east of the airport: trains either stop at the Airport Transit Centre (local and some express services) or continue forward to the '''Areza Concourse''' station, located at the Areza Concourse of Terminal C (express services only). This arrangement allows Line 9 express passengers travelling to or from Areza to bypass the main terminal concourse entirely, while local passengers bound for the city use the Airport Transit Centre.

=== Road ===

[[File:Sant Cristofor Airport E51 approach placeholder.jpg|thumb|250px|The E51 approach to the airport from Original]]

The airport is connected to the city road network via the '''E51''', which runs east from [[Original (ciutat)|Original]] to the airport. The E51 connects to the [[Eastern Highway, Sant Cristòfor|Eastern Highway]] (E52), the elevated expressway running through Original, providing onward access to the city centre and the wider road network. Journey time by road to Original is approximately 25–40 minutes depending on traffic. Taxi, ride-hailing, and private vehicle access is available at all terminals. Long-term and short-term parking is provided in multi-storey car parks adjacent to each terminal.

The '''[[E54 expressway]]''' is a dedicated road connecting the Areza Concourse of Terminal C directly to the [[International City of Areza]]. The E54 has no intermediate junctions and no access to the Balboan road network; vehicles using it may only travel between the airport and Areza, and are not permitted to stop in Balboa. Access to the E54 is restricted to authorised vehicles: [[Adonian Community]] government vehicles, chartered car services, and scheduled bus services. Private vehicles are not permitted on the E54 or at the Areza Concourse.

=== Bus ===

The [[Autoritat de Transport de Sant Cristòfor]] (ATS) operates airport bus routes connecting the airport to major hotels, the cruise terminal, and the ciutats not served by the Metro. Airport bus services depart from the ground transportation centre beneath the central atrium.

== Accidents and incidents ==

[[File:Sant Cristofor Airport control tower placeholder.jpg|thumb|250px|The airport control tower, with Runway 09/27 in the background]]

* '''14 February 1988''' — [[Aeroístmus]] Flight 107, a [[Boeing 737-200|Boeing 737]] arriving from [[Sant Bart]] with 112 passengers and 6 crew, overran Runway 09/27 on landing during a heavy rainstorm. The aircraft came to rest 140 metres beyond the runway threshold, its nose gear collapsing on the soft ground. All 118 occupants evacuated safely via emergency slides; 9 passengers sustained minor injuries. The investigation attributed the overrun to aquaplaning on the rain-soaked runway and a tailwind component that exceeded the airline's landing limits. Following the incident, the Balboa Airports Authority installed grooved surface treatment on both runways and revised wet-weather landing minima.

* '''3 September 1993''' — A runway incursion occurred when a [[RapidAir (Balboa)|RapidAir]] Boeing 737 entered Runway 09/27 without clearance while a [[Aeroístmus]] Airbus A310 was on its take-off roll. The A310's crew aborted take-off at approximately 120 knots, stopping approximately 400 metres short of the intersecting RapidAir aircraft. The investigation found that the RapidAir crew had misinterpreted a taxi clearance as a line-up clearance, and that the air traffic controller's phraseology had been ambiguous. The incident prompted the Balboa Airports Authority to implement mandatory readback procedures for all runway entry clearances and to install enhanced taxiway lighting.

* '''22 November 2001''' — [[Volisanian Airlines]] Flight 614, an [[Airbus A300|Airbus A300-600]] arriving from [[Volisania]] with 187 passengers and 12 crew, suffered a collapse of the left main landing gear on touchdown on Runway 09/27. The aircraft veered left onto the grass shoulder, coming to rest at an angle to the runway. All 199 occupants evacuated via emergency slides; 22 passengers and 2 crew members sustained injuries, none life-threatening. The investigation determined that the landing gear had suffered a fatigue fracture in the side strut, a known issue on the A300-600 that had been the subject of an airworthiness directive. The aircraft was written off. The incident accelerated the retirement of the A300-600 from the Volisanian Airlines fleet.

* '''7 June 2006''' — A bird strike on a [[Aeroístmus]] Boeing 767 departing for [[Portnou]] caused both engines to surge during the initial climb. The crew returned the aircraft to the airport and landed safely on Runway 09/27. The subsequent inspection found significant damage to both engine fan blades from a flock of large seabirds. The incident led to the implementation of a wildlife hazard management programme at the airport, including habitat modification around the airfield and radar-assisted bird detection systems.

== Relationship with other airports ==

{{main|Sant Cristòfor Els Aiguamolls Airport}}

[[Sant Cristòfor Els Aiguamolls Airport]], located in the neighbouring [[Els Aiguamolls]] comarca just north of the city boundary, serves as a complementary facility rather than a relief airport. Els Aiguamolls handles domestic and short-haul regional routes, and is used primarily by residents of the northern ciutats — particularly [[Costa Nord (ciutat)|Costa Nord]] — seeking connections to [[Sant Bart]] and [[Nurra]] without transiting the busier Sant Cristòfor International. [[Aeroístmus]] operates services from Els Aiguamolls, and the airport is connected to the city by commuter rail. The two airports are not formally coordinated but serve distinct markets: Sant Cristòfor International for long-haul and high-density domestic operations, and Els Aiguamolls for domestic point-to-point and regional services.

